<title>SINGAPORE: ST Aerospace signs US$21 mln contract.</title>
<headline>ST Aerospace signs US$21 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Technologies Aerospace Ltd said on Monday its commercial aircraft maintenance arm, ST Aviation Services Co, signed a US$21 million contract with Northwest Airlines for the modification of nine Boeing 747-200 aircraft.</p>
<p>The contract also stipulates an option for the modification for another six Boeing 747-200 aircraft, the company said in a statement. It did give an estimate of the value of the option.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
